From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude Haiku 5.5" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 05:01:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] A query for an install folder creates no folder

installdir() created the folder of a package every time it was called
without readonly, and xmake calls it that way while it registers the
requirements of a project and while it reports them with --info. So a
configure left an empty folder for each build hash it asked about, and
the next query took that folder for an install. Only a call with a
subdirectory creates the folder now. The install action creates the
install folder itself once it has cleared it, so the install scripts
still find it.

Self-review: clean
Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Changes-build-output: no

---
 xmake/core/package/package.lua                                | 2 +-
 xmake/modules/private/action/require/impl/actions/install.lua | 1 +
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/xmake/core/package/package.lua b/xmake/core/package/package.lua
index 682cafce4..a4499b861 100644
--- a/xmake/core/package/package.lua
+++ b/xmake/core/package/package.lua
@@ -987,7 +987,7 @@ function _instance:installdir(...)
     if opt and opt.readonly then
         return dir
     end
-    if not os.isdir(dir)then
+    if #dirs > 0 and not os.isdir(dir) then
         os.mkdir(dir)
     end
     return dir
diff --git a/xmake/modules/private/action/require/impl/actions/install.lua b/xmake/modules/private/action/require/impl/actions/install.lua
index 3a6d2af51..c2fd45ef7 100644
--- a/xmake/modules/private/action/require/impl/actions/install.lua
+++ b/xmake/modules/private/action/require/impl/actions/install.lua
@@ -567,6 +567,7 @@ function main(package)
 
                     -- clear install directory
                     _clear_installdir(package)
+                    os.mkdir(package:installdir())
 
                     -- download package resources
                     download_resources(package)
